            "description": "Press a key or chord (xdotool-style DSL, e.g. \"return\", \"cmd+a\", \"cmd+shift+t\"). Requires app or pid. Focus must be on the target. Cursor-safe; background.",
            "inputSchema": {
              "properties": {
                "activate": {
                  "description": "FALLBACK ONLY — avoid unless needed. press_key posts keys in the background by default, which lands even when the target window is fully covered by other windows (verified for native apps on macOS 26). Setting this briefly raises a fully covered window (a visible flash) to flush input for apps that drop occluded keys. Default false = pure background, never raises. Try a normal press_key first; only set activate:true if the key did not land.",
